## Configure Slurm on the Compute Nodes

Point each compute node's `slurmd` at the head node (configless mode) and enable
it. The setting is written before the service is enabled, so a stateful node
that applies this after boot starts `slurmd` with it already in place.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure Slurm on the compute nodes -->
```bash
# Register the Slurm server with the computes (configless mode)
{{ compute_run("echo SLURMD_OPTIONS=--conf-server ${sms_ip} > /etc/sysconfig/slurmd") }}
{{ compute_service_enable("slurmd.service") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
{%- if is_xcat_stateless %}

The image carries no munge key, so at boot `munge` and `slurmd` start before the
synclist delivers it. xCAT runs a file's `.post` script on a node whenever the
synclist updates that file there, so a script next to the key restarts both
once the key arrives, and again whenever a new key is synced with
`updatenode -F`:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Restart munge and slurmd when the synclist delivers a new munge key -->
```bash
cat > /etc/munge/munge.key.post << 'EOF'
#!/bin/sh
systemctl restart munge.service slurmd.service
EOF
chmod 700 /etc/munge/munge.key.post
echo "EXECUTE:" >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
echo "/etc/munge/munge.key.post" >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
{%- endif %}
